From 8e455df26a4cc68910ad0b9dffe66a4f8542eb39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:27:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): publish the park, honour SCHEDULED_UNTIL
 offsets, require a wake reason [daveey]

Desktop showed every scheduled card on another gateway as "a producer the owner did not publish": the owner
record never carried the park.

- kanban_wait_replica.published_park: awaiting (verbatim), wake_check (<=500) and park {wake_at, reason, ended_at,
  outcome} of a live park; observe_owner_task adds them for scheduled cards and blocked kind=time cards, before the
  observation hash.
- Both remote-card projections (_park_of in kanban_origin_ledger and kanban_session_activity) now prefer the
  published park over the last run's fields; in links_reader=replica mode replica_cards copies the owner-published
  wait fields from the origin-ledger card when the ledger reports the same status (Board replica rows carry none).
- kanban_wait_info.park_fields: SCHEDULED_UNTIL accepts Z / +HH:MM / -HH:MM and honours it (naive stays UTC).
- kanban_awaiting: a timed park naming nothing (no awaiting, no wake_check, no live card) is refused
  no_wake_reason, with the fix in the message; only a short continue (<=2 h pacing) stays an inferred clock. A
  soak text still gets soak_wait first. System clock parks declare a why (placement forward requeue, shared-blocker
  cadence). Tool/CLI help says a wake reason is required; the dashboard PATCH/bulk bodies accept awaiting.
- Tests: published fields per park kind, labels through both projections, offsets, no_wake_reason on every entry
  path, system parks, continued-park regression; existing tests that parked bare clocks now declare one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
